  "why": "Grades retrieval on a repository nobody here wrote. The seventy questions in repo_queries.json are asked about this project's own source, by the party that wrote both the code and its descriptions, over an index where every unit under src/ carries a hand-written bilingual description. That is the warmest case there is and it cannot see what a first-time user sees: a foreign repository, zero descriptions, and a vocabulary nobody here chose.",
  "caveat": "The questions are phrased in a user's words on purpose, not in the words of the docstring that answers them, so a hit means retrieval bridged a paraphrase rather than echoing a string it was handed. Every acceptable answer is checked against the index before anything is scored.",
